|~ `::excerpt`, the kind of the facts a host tells of a failure past its
   rooms, and what is declared under it: its laws.
   The rules it holds: [QSPRN#excerpt], [QSERR#alert]. ~|

:excerpt
  |~~ An excerpt tells the facts of a failure a host prints past the room
      of a fact, under the tag of its refusal,
      `::number/add/AddendKindNotTakenError::excerpt{…}`. Each fact stands
      whole within three hundred characters. Past them stands the cell the
      host keeps it in, `:addend/found ::cell"…"`. Beside the cell stand
      its tag and the views the kind of the fact reveals that fit the
      room, each under the name of the fact and its own,
      `:addend/found/tag ::vec` and `:addend/found/count 3410`. Beside them
      stand its parts, each by the same rule under the name of the fact and
      its own. A map stands by its keys, an error at rest and an excerpt by
      their facts, and a value under a tag its kind does not wire by the
      parts of what it holds, whose tag stands under `payload/tag`,
      `:answer/payload/tag`. A vector, a set, a string, a quote and a doc
      stand as their views. A key is the chain a reader types,
      `:answer/addend/found/count` read as
      `::cell"…" | answer | addend | found | count`. A host that keeps no
      cell shows the tag, the views and the parts alone. No fact is cut: it
      stands whole, as a cell that gives it back whole, or as the facts its
      kind reveals of it. Where the alert passes its room, the entries laid
      deepest and last drop until it fits, each whole in the failure `!|`
      reads.

      An excerpt is a map under its tag, read by its keys, and the kind of
      the refusal over it reads its facts by their names, a cell standing
      for any fact; `raise` refuses it, a failure told and not held. The
      whole is read live, a fact of a failure by `!|` and a cell by
      `answer`.
      ::link~(::kind/reveals) ::link~(::cell)
      ::link~(::qlang/hosts)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts |~~ The facts told, whole, as cells or as views. ~~| ::map
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ An excerpt is the map of the facts a host tells of a failure,
            `::excerpt{:addend/found ::cell"…" :addend/found/count 3410}`.
        ~~|
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesAVector
        |~~ An excerpt is a map of facts, no vector. ~~|
        ~(::excerpt[1] !| tag | eq ::excerpt/PayloadKindNotTakenError)
    | proves :readsBackAsItself
        |~~ An excerpt prints and reads back as itself. ~~|
        ~(::excerpt{:addend/found ::cell"f410f1df625c" :addend/found/count 3410}
          | eq (print | parse | answer))
    | proves :readsAViewByItsKey
        |~~ A view stands under the name of its fact and its own. ~~|
        ~(::excerpt{:addend/found/count 3410} | get /:addend/found/count
          | eq 3410);
